{"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/WorldModule\/documentation\/WorldModule","doc:\/\/WorldModule\/documentation\/WorldModule\/World"]]},"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/WorldModule\/documentation\/WorldModule\/World\/runConcurrently(_:)"},"schemaVersion":{"patch":0,"major":0,"minor":3},"kind":"symbol","sections":[],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Runs changes at the same time, each on its own copy of the world, and keeps what each one"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"wrote."}],"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"languages":["swift"],"platforms":["Linux"],"tokens":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"mutating"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"runConcurrently"},{"text":"(","kind":"text"},{"text":"_","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"changes","kind":"internalParam"},{"text":": [","kind":"text"},{"text":"ConcurrentChange","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:11WorldModule16ConcurrentChangeV","identifier":"doc:\/\/WorldModule\/documentation\/WorldModule\/ConcurrentChange"},{"text":"])","kind":"text"}]}]},{"kind":"parameters","parameters":[{"name":"changes","content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The changes to run.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]}]},{"content":[{"anchor":"discussion","level":2,"text":"Discussion","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Use this method to spread independent work across the processor’s cores. Each change reads"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the world as it was before any of them ran, and writes only the types its access lists, so"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the result is the same as running the changes one after another in any order:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"syntax":"swift","code":["var world = World()","let ball = world.spawn(Position(x: 0, y: 0), Velocity(dx: 1, dy: 0), Health(current: 10))","","world.runConcurrently([","    ConcurrentChange(access: .reads(Velocity.self).writes(Position.self)) { world in","        world.update(Position.self, reading: Velocity.self) { position, row in","            position.x += row.components.dx","        }","    },","    ConcurrentChange(access: .writes(Health.self)) { world in","        world.update(Health.self) { health, _ in health.current -= 1 }","    },","])","","print(world[Position.self, of: ball].x, world[Health.self, of: ball].current)","\/\/ Prints \"1.0 9\""],"type":"codeListing"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A change sees the components and resources that other changes write as missing, so its"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"access must list everything it reads. Command buffers a change queues with ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/WorldModule\/documentation\/WorldModule\/World\/queue(_:)","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"are queued in this world in the order of ","type":"text"},{"code":"changes","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"style":"important","name":"Important","content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A change must write only the component and resource types its access lists,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"and must not spawn or despawn entities. It writes relations through their "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/WorldModule\/documentation\/WorldModule\/Targets","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"components, and the hierarchy through "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Targets<ChildOf>"},{"type":"text","text":"."}]}],"type":"aside"},{"style":"note","name":"Complexity","content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"O("},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"c","type":"text"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"text":"·","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"t"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"text":"), besides the cost of the changes themselves, where ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"c"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"text":" is the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"number of changes and ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"t"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"text":" is the number of component types the world has stored.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],"type":"aside"},{"style":"note","name":"Precondition","content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"No two accesses conflict, and each change writes only what its access"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"lists and spawns and despawns nothing; a change that breaks this traps. In debug builds,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"a change that reads a component or resource type its access doesn’t list traps too. Any"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"change may read "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/WorldModule\/documentation\/WorldModule\/Disabled","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/WorldModule\/documentation\/WorldModule\/Prefab","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"type":"paragraph"}],"type":"aside"}],"kind":"content"}],"metadata":{"modules":[{"name":"WorldModule"}],"fragments":[{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"runConcurrently","kind":"identifier"},{"kind":"text","text":"(["},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:11WorldModule16ConcurrentChangeV","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"ConcurrentChange"},{"kind":"text","text":"])"}],"externalID":"s:11WorldModule0A0V15runConcurrentlyyySayAA16ConcurrentChangeVGF","extendedModule":"WorldModule","roleHeading":"Instance Method","role":"symbol","title":"runConcurrently(_:)","remoteSource":{"fileName":"Concurrency.swift","url":"https:\/\/github.com\/Tyler-Keith-Thompson\/ECS\/blob\/main\/Sources\/WorldModule\/Concurrency.swift#L264"},"symbolKind":"method"},"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/worldmodule\/world\/runconcurrently(_:)"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"references":{"doc://WorldModule/documentation/WorldModule/Disabled":{"navigatorTitle":[{"text":"Disabled","kind":"identifier"}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A component that makes queries and updates skip an entity, unless they ask for it."}],"role":"symbol","type":"topic","kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/WorldModule\/documentation\/WorldModule\/Disabled","url":"\/documentation\/worldmodule\/disabled","fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Disabled","kind":"identifier"}],"title":"Disabled"},"doc://WorldModule/documentation/WorldModule/World/applyQueuedCommands()":{"abstract":[{"text":"Applies every queued command buffer, in the order the buffers were queued, and empties the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"queue.","type":"text"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/WorldModule\/documentation\/WorldModule\/World\/applyQueuedCommands()","type":"topic","role":"symbol","title":"applyQueuedCommands()","kind":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/worldmodule\/world\/applyqueuedcommands()","fragments":[{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"applyQueuedCommands","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"() -> [","kind":"text"},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Entity","preciseIdentifier":"s:11WorldModule6EntityV"},{"kind":"text","text":"]"}]},"doc://WorldModule/documentation/WorldModule/World/runConcurrently(_:)":{"abstract":[{"text":"Runs changes at the same time, each on its own copy of the world, and keeps what each one","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"wrote.","type":"text"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/WorldModule\/documentation\/WorldModule\/World\/runConcurrently(_:)","type":"topic","role":"symbol","kind":"symbol","title":"runConcurrently(_:)","url":"\/documentation\/worldmodule\/world\/runconcurrently(_:)","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":